{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## PHASE 2 REPORT — rebar-debug complete; Gerrit gates pending\n\n**Problem:** the present scc grounding metric backend could never emit per-file oversize matches.\n\n**Proven root cause:** `src/rebar/grounding/engine_b_backends.py::_metric_invoke` invoked `scc --format json <repo>` without `--by-file`. scc 3.7.0 returned language summaries whose `Files` arrays were empty; `_scc_files` therefore yielded no entries and the threshold loop never ran.\n\n**Proof:** a runtime trace through `_run_metric` captured the exact argv, 27 zero-length `Files` arrays, and `records=[]`. The same binary/repository with `--by-file` returned 2,912 entries, including 29 with `Code > 800`, ruling out parser and threshold alternatives.\n\n**Test/TDD:** `tests/unit/grounding/test_engine_b.py::test_metric_backend_requests_per_file_json_and_emits_only_over_cutoff` crosses `_run_metric -> _metric_invoke -> harness boundary -> JSON parser -> _scc_files -> ev.match` with an argv-faithful scc fake. Its preconditions prove 801- and 800-line inputs. In final form it was collected and observed RED first (`0 != 1` matches), physically removed from the worktree, and withheld from the fixer. The fixer saw only the RCA/reproduction/contract card. Restored afterward, it was GREEN on the first repair attempt. Defect-seeded mutation (remove `--by-file`) returned it to the same RED; restoring the fix returned GREEN. The refactoring litmus removed irrelevant flag-order coupling, then the revised final oracle was re-proven RED without the fix and GREEN with it. Timeout, nonzero exit, invalid JSON, and absent-tool fail-open paths are covered and green.\n\n**Fix:** commit `0cc74619ec405ad2927b7ad451aed416dcc664b5` adds the one required scc argument; no threshold, `Code` field, evidence shape, or failure behavior changed. Repair attempts: 1.\n\n**Scope/safety:** bounded caller sweep found `_metric_invoke` called only by `_run_metric`; Engine B scan/oracle consumers expect evidence matches and none relies on the empty result. This restores the built-in detector contract, creates no API or capability, adds no dependency, and weakens no test. Signed plan-review PASS was current before Phase 2.\n\n**Verification:** focused held-out/failure coverage 5 passed; focused grounding cohort passed; `make check` passed (ruff, format, complexity, workflow checks, mypy); CI-equivalent default suite passed `13,535 passed, 52 skipped` in 797.44s. Original live `_run_metric(Path(\".\"))` now emits 29 normalized matches, including real over-800 files.\n\n**Sibling sweeps:** construct sweep found exactly two production consumers that parse scc `Files`: grounding (fixed here) and `src/rebar/metrics/analyzers/scc_loc.py`, which already has the documented `--by-file` requirement from closed bug rapid-cuboid-velvetcrab. No unfixed construct sibling. Parity rule: per-file scc consumers must explicitly request per-file JSON. CLI/MCP have no independent metric implementation; library grounding oracle, code review, plan review, and criterion preview all route through shared Engine B; the separate metrics analyzer is already correct; no mirror direction applies. No MISSING surface.\n\n**Residual warning dispositions:** existing open owners: `unamicable-exuberant-chupacabra` (enrich-drain >20ms) and `ferrety-crippling-dairycow` (Pydantic unresolved lifespan). Newly filed+linked for dedicated debug: `treelike-unamusing-grosbeak` (Python 3.14 tar filter), `stumpy-cinnabar-basenji` (multithreaded fork/deadlock warning), `dragonish-sylphic-sheep` (OpenAI prefix v2 semantic change; decision brief recorded, no implementation pending approval), and `socialized-exclusive-mouse` (Pydantic event-loop warning; handed to the separate RP-01 session).\n\n**Landing:** Gerrit 1829, patch set 1. Local code-review capability is disabled; authoritative LLM-Review and Verified gates are running. Ticket remains in_progress until both are +1, the change is submitted, and origin/main contains the merge."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786915180763977001,"uuid":"f36f5bfd-70f5-405c-92bd-79bf7d6ad4de"}